---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Choose a Personal Injury Attorney in Florida"
  description="Learn what to look for when hiring a personal injury attorney in Florida — experience, fees, communication, and track record."
  canonical="https://www.findpiattorney.com/how-to-choose-a-pi-attorney/"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1">
    <section class="bg-brand-900 text-white">
      <div class="page-container py-12">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">How to Choose a Personal Injury Attorney</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-brand-200 max-w-2xl">Key factors to consider when hiring a PI attorney in Florida.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="page-container section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-gray">
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          Choosing the right personal injury attorney can significantly impact the outcome of your case. Here's what to consider before hiring.
        </p>

        <h2 class="!text-2xl !font-bold !text-brand-900 !mt-8 !mb-4">Verify Florida Bar Membership</h2>
        <p>Always verify that any attorney you consider is an active, licensed member of The Florida Bar in good standing. You can look up any attorney using this directory or directly on the <a href="https://www.floridabar.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Florida Bar website</a>.</p>

        <h2 class="!text-2xl !font-bold !text-brand-900 !mt-8 !mb-4">Look for Personal Injury Experience</h2>
        <p>Personal injury law is specialized. Look for attorneys who focus primarily on PI cases — not general practitioners who handle everything. Experience with your specific type of case (car accidents, slip and fall, medical malpractice, etc.) matters.</p>

        <h2 class="!text-2xl !font-bold !text-brand-900 !mt-8 !mb-4">Understand the Fee Structure</h2>
        <p>Most personal injury attorneys work on a <strong>contingency fee basis</strong> — meaning they only get paid if you win. Typical contingency fees in Florida range from 33% to 40% of the recovery. Make sure you understand all fees before signing any agreement.</p>

        <h2 class="!text-2xl !font-bold !text-brand-900 !mt-8 !mb-4">Assess Communication Style</h2>
        <p>Your attorney should be accessible, responsive, and willing to explain the process clearly. During your initial consultation, assess:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>How promptly do they respond to calls or emails?</li>
          <li>Do they explain things in plain language?</li>
          <li>Do they listen carefully to your situation?</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="!text-2xl !font-bold !text-brand-900 !mt-8 !mb-4">Check Reviews and Track Record</h2>
        <p>Research the attorney's reputation through online reviews, peer ratings, and any available case results. While past results don't guarantee future outcomes, a consistent track record demonstrates competence.</p>

        <h2 class="!text-2xl !font-bold !text-brand-900 !mt-8 !mb-4">Act Quickly — Florida's Statute of Limitations</h2>
        <p>Florida's statute of limitations for personal injury cases is <strong>2 years</strong> from the date of injury. Don't delay — important evidence can disappear, and witnesses' memories fade over time.</p>

        <div class="not-prose mt-10 p-6 bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-xl text-center">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-900 mb-2">Find a Personal Injury Attorney</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Browse our directory of licensed Florida attorneys by city.</p>
          <a href="/personal-injury-attorneys/florida" class="btn-primary text-sm">Browse by City</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
